# Supervised detectors + feature ablation (offline, post-hoc)

Rows: benign train 385200, benign cal 270000, benign holdout 366000; attack cal 7200, attack holdout 7200; rollup look-alike (cal+holdout) 12000; hard look-alike (holdout) 2400; price tiers 30.
Attack feature vectors: distinct (gas_limit,bytecode_size,opcode_count,wei) combos = 1; distinct gas_price tiers = 30 -> effective n of the attack class is 30 tier points, not 14400 rows.
- attack: gas_limit=[8000000.] bytecode_size=[98372.] opcode_count=[129234.] wei=[0.]
- rollup look-alike: gas_limit=[2151000.] bytecode_size=[98372.] opcode_count=[129234.] wei=[0.]
- hard look-alike: gas_limit=[8000000.] bytecode_size=[98372.] opcode_count=[129234.] wei=[0.]
- identical wire fields attack vs hard look-alike (gas_limit,wei,bytecode_size): True; attack vs rollup: False

Cols: AUROC_ben = attack vs benign(cal+holdout); AUROC_roll/hard = P(attack score > look-alike score) (0.5 = inseparable); TPR@thr = holdout attack flagged at threshold = 99th pct of benign-calibration scores; FPR_cal/FPR_ho = benign flag rate; flag_roll/hard = look-alike flag rate; bytes-wtd TPR over synthetic size grid (3k..98k). Brackets = 95% bootstrap over price tiers (n=tiers, tiny effective n).


